---
description: Android / Google Play release safety for the mobile app
globs: apps/mobile/**
alwaysApply: false
---

- Follow docs/PLAY_STORE.md. Target API level 36+ is required by Google Play; never lower it.
- Never change the Android `applicationId`/package name, signing config or keystores. Ask first.
- Do not hand-edit generated `android/` folders; change `app.config.*` / config plugins instead (ADR for native code).
- Permissions: request the minimum, only at the moment of use, and list each one in the PR description.
- Secrets never go in `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` variables: they are bundled into the app.
- Support edge-to-edge and predictive back; test on an API 36 emulator and one low-end device.
- Any feature creating accounts must include in-app account deletion.
- Version codes are auto-incremented by EAS; never hand-edit them.
